UID:event_315965806@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050444Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T120000
SUMMARY:Beyond Chatbots: Build Your First Production Agent with Microsoft 
 Foundry
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nAI agents are rapidly moving beyond
  simple conversational experiences. In this session\, we will build the fo
 undation of a production-ready agent using Microsoft Foundry Agent Service
 \, Microsoft Agent Framework\, and Azure application services.\n\nStarting
  from a practical enterprise operations scenario\, we will define the agen
 t’s responsibilities\, instructions\, tools\, conversation state\, and s
 tructured outputs. We will then connect the agent to a Foundry model\, add
  a typed function tool\, stream responses to a web application\, and exami
 ne the architectural differences between a model call\, an assistant\, an 
 agent\, and an agent workflow.\n\nThe session will also explore hosting op
 tions\, including Foundry hosted agents and custom agent applications depl
 oyed to Azure Container Apps. Along the way\, we will discuss identity\, c
 onfiguration\, state management\, failure boundaries\, and the design deci
 sions that separate a useful prototype from an application that can evolve
  toward production.\n\nBy the end of the session\, attendees will understa
 nd the core components of a Microsoft Foundry agent application and will h
 ave a reusable starting point for building their own agentic solutions. Ke
 y topics: Microsoft Foundry Agent Service Microsoft Agent Framework Agent 
 instructions and tool contracts Conversation state and streaming responses
  Structured outputs Hosted agents and Azure Container Apps Production-orie
 nted agent architecture
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3159
 65806/
